a signal a thread raises: faulthandler's"] [312 1 "// fatal handler (then death by it), its user handler (then, chained, the Python handler or the default action), or the"] [313 1 "// default action that ends the process when the signal's Python disposition is SIG_DFL (Go's runtime would ignore"] [314 1 "// SIGUSR1 and print its own traceback for SIGABRT)."] [344 1 "// fhStart starts the goroutines of the fatal and user signals once."] [374 1 "// fhGetFileno is faulthandler_get_fileno: None or absent sys.stderr, an int a descriptor, else file.fileno() (the file"] [375 1 "// flushed); the file kept while it is used (nil for a descriptor)."] [420 28 "// a flush error ignored"] [424 1 "// fhIntArg is the 'i' format: PyLong_AsInt."] [432 1 "// fhBoolArg is the 'p' format: PyObject_IsTrue; absent the default."] [440 1 "// fhTimeoutHeader is format_timeout."] [465 1 "// fhTimeoutUs is _PyTime_FromSecondsObject then _PyTime_AsMicroseconds, both _PyTime_ROUND_TIMEOUT (up)."] [496 1 "// fhCancelLater is cancel_dump_traceback_later: the watchdog stopped and waited for."] [643 29 "// the watchdog has no Python thread: no \"Current thread\""] [695 53 "// sigaction refuses SIGKILL and SIGSTOP"] [725 45 "// the Python handler's notification, which Reset removed"] [749 78 "// the overflow's SIGSEGV on the alternate stack"] [751 3 "// Py_FatalError in a thread without a Python thread state: the message, the threads (none current), the C"] [752 3 "// stack, then abort() with faulthandler finalized (no second traceback)"] [776 1 "// faulthandlerAtStart is _PyFaulthandler_Init(enable): -X faulthandler or PYTHONFAULTHANDLER set and not empty"] [777 1 "// import faulthandler and call its enable()."]] :go/pos {:name [3 9] :package [3 1]} :go/semis [[139 19] [159 16] [159 18] [169 14] [248 51] [249 61] [260 58] [264 36] [290 25] [338 35] [351 35] [379 72] [388 32] [389 31] [390 84] [412 22] [413 26] [426 25] [467 22] [476 28] [605 35] [610 33]]} (go/file "builtins_faulthandler.go" :build 